    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0530" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg458"/>

                <head>No. 275.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Hamlin</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 20,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 195, of the 2d
                    November last, to your predecessor, and to my instruction of the 10th instant, I
                    inclose a copy of a letter furnishing additional particulars of the levy of a
                    charge of 10 cents per ton on cargoes for Spanish ports by Spanish consuls in
                    this country.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>





